{
  "sn51.14:0.1": "Linked Discourses 51.14 ",
  "sn51.14:0.2": "2. Shaking the Stilt Longhouse ",
  "sn51.14:0.3": "With Moggallāna ",
  "sn51.14:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "sn51.14:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in the stilt longhouse of Migāra’s mother in the Eastern Monastery. ",
  "sn51.14:1.3": "Now at that time several mendicants were staying beneath the longhouse. They were haughty, insolent, fickle, scurrilous, loose-tongued, unmindful, lacking situational awareness and immersion, with straying minds and undisciplined faculties. ",
  "sn51.14:2.1": "Then the Buddha addressed Venerable Mahāmoggallāna, ",
  "sn51.14:2.2": "“These spiritual companions of yours staying beneath the longhouse are haughty, insolent, fickle, scurrilous, loose-tongued, unmindful, lacking situational awareness and immersion, with straying minds and undisciplined faculties. ",
  "sn51.14:2.3": "Go, Moggallāna, and strike awe in those mendicants!” ",
  "sn51.14:3.1": "“Yes, sir,” replied Mahāmoggallāna. Then he used his psychic power to make the longhouse shake and rock and tremble with his big toe. ",
  "sn51.14:3.2": "Then those mendicants stood to one side, shocked and awestruck. ",
  "sn51.14:3.3": "“Oh lord, how incredible, how amazing! ",
  "sn51.14:3.4": "There’s no wind at all; and this stilt longhouse of Migāra’s mother has deep foundations. It’s firmly embedded, imperturbable and unshakable. And yet it shakes and rocks and quivers!” ",
  "sn51.14:4.1": "Then the Bu